# Dashboard CSS — Tailwind first, module files

## Styling priority (dashboard / gestion)

1. **Tailwind utilities** in Razor (via `Styles/app.css` `@theme` tokens: `bg-surface`, `border-line`, `text-pine`, etc.).
2. **Shared dashboard CSS** for patterns reused across modules (lists, forms, shell).
3. **Module CSS file** when a Vente/Achat/Opérationnel page needs layout or behavior Tailwind cannot express cleanly (e.g. table → mobile cards, autocomplete dropdowns).
4. **Never** add one-off rules to a monolithic layout file — use the module file.

## File layout (mirrors `Views/`)

```
Styles/
├── app.css                    ← Tailwind entry + @import chain
├── Shared/
│   ├── _tokens.css            ← colors, spacing (single hex source)
│   ├── _DashboardLayout.css   ← barrel @import only
│   ├── _DashboardShell.css    ← topbar, sidebar, dash-main
│   ├── _DashboardLists.css    ← .list-*, pagination, mobile list cards
│   ├── _DashboardForms.css    ← .form-*, .dash-alert
│   └── _DashboardUtilities.css
├── Vente/
│   ├── Clients.css            ← client-only overrides
│   └── Devis.css              ← .doc-* document forms + mobile line cards
├── Achat/                     ← (future module CSS)
└── Operationnel/
    └── OpsPages.css
```

When adding a new dashboard module:

1. Create `Styles/{Section}/{Module}.css` (e.g. `Styles/Vente/BonsCommande.css`).
2. Add `@import "../{Section}/{Module}.css";` to `Shared/_DashboardLayout.css`.
3. Reuse shared `.list-*` / `.form-*` before inventing new class names.

## Tailwind vs custom CSS

| Use Tailwind | Use module CSS |
|--------------|----------------|
| Page spacing, flex/grid one-offs | Complex responsive table → card transforms |
| Typography with `@theme` fonts | `data-label` + `::before` mobile list/card rows |
| Simple borders/backgrounds on wrappers | Autocomplete dropdown positioning |
| `@apply` in `@layer components` for **global** primitives (`.btn-gold`, `.dash-panel`) | Document line tables with many column widths |

**Tokens:** custom CSS must use `var(--…)` from `_tokens.css` — no hardcoded hex. Tailwind `@theme` mirrors the same tokens.

## Build

After CSS changes: `npm run css:build` in `src/OliveMorocco.Web` (or `dotnet build`).

Do **not** edit `wwwroot/css/site.css` directly.
